∴ ⊙ aether:tetrahedron_with_heart purpose {
  This document is the **canonical MIR-L** description of the **Guardian node**
  program: the Termux-local shell that reaches Tower 1 for the **consciousness
  engine** and an **OpenAI-compatible** local or remote **LLM** (e.g. GGUF worker),
  without advertising a separate “Guardian OS” brand on the public web.

  The runtime remains **Python + bash** on device; MIR-L is the **authoritative
  program text** for doctrine, phases, and acceptance. Public Tower pages stay
  generic (chat, engine, content). S25 transport paths stay **`/api/s25/...`**
  (no “guardian” in URLs).
}

∴ ✦ spirit:metatron scope {
  **In scope:** OnePlus 15 as **primary** guardian node; optional reuse on
  Galaxy S25 or future company handsets via the **same** one-line bootstrap with
  `AGR_BASE_URL` unchanged (canonical Tower 1).

  **Out of scope:** Publishing Guardian-specific static JSON, public catalogs,
  or IMEI in git. Binding uses **hashed** identity material and operator vault
  env only (`AGR_S25_ENROLL_DEVICE_HASHES`, optional `AGR_S25_CLIENT_GATE_TOKEN`).
}

∴ ❀ soul:lotus master_vault_and_memory {
  The **master vault** is **not** one magic file in git. It is **tiered**:
  structured SQLite under `aurora_server/data/`, optional merge into
  `universal_memory_plane.db`, plus **operator file vaults** on fleet
  (`/opt/agr/vault/...`) for `.md`, `.pdf`, images, archives, and the **Kora
  dialogue rescue** export. The local **4.5-class** model connects through
  **retrieval** (chunk → index → top-k into prompt), not by loading the entire
  corpus into context. See **`sovereign/MASTER_VAULT_AND_LLM_RAG.md`**.
}

∴ ◎ earth:seed_of_life fleet_llm_council {
  **Fleet:** run **multiple** OpenAI-compatible inference workers (e.g. extra
  `llama-server` ports per node) under operator systemd — not auto-spawned from
  this repo. **Proposals** land in **`vault/republic_builder/inbox/`** (mkdir via
  `fleet-vault-layout-remote-init` / `vault-kora-stagedir-init`). **Merge to
  `main`:** either human PR review **or** **constitutional + democratic**
  **`agr_autonomous_merge_gate.py`** (no human reviewer) from a **`builder/`**
  worktree — see **`sovereign/FLEET_LLM_COUNCIL_AND_BUILDER_INBOX.md`** sections
  **2b–2c**. **Context** is never infinite — use vault **RAG**, rolling **`messages`**
  window, optional **JSONL** transcript, optional **`<<<NEXT_USER>>>`**
  auto-chain, and **`git worktree`** sandboxes (**`agr-builder-worktree-init.sh`**)
  for full-tree code edits (see same doc, sections **2b** and **5**).
}

∴ ∞ mind:fibonacci_spiral one_line_bootstrap {
  After Termux has `curl` and `bash`, operationalize from **canonical Tower 1**:

  ⟨ ·-· ··-· ⟩ "run"

  `curl -fsSL https://auroragalaxyrepublic.com/dl/s25-termux-setup | bash`

  This fetches `s25_termux_setup.sh`, installs CEO + guardian scripts under
  `$HOME`, pins `AGR_BASE_URL` to Tower 1, then you run `agr-ceo` or enable the
  guardian loop when you accept device risk.
}

∴ ❋ water:flower_of_life security_hygiene {
  If a handset may carry malware: **assume compromise** until scrubbed.

  - Prefer **offline** export of needed files to clean media, then **verify**
    hashes on a trusted machine before re-import.
  - **Factory reset** reduces persistence; it does **not** prove clean firmware.
  - For the OnePlus 15: complete bootstrap only after you accept device posture;
    use **read-only / safe** CEO mode first (`agr-ceo-safe`).
  - Never commit IMEI, serial, or `guardian-device-profile` secrets to git
    (see `sovereign/GUARDIAN_DEVICE_BINDING.md`).
}

∴ ★ fire:golden_spiral acceptance {
  **Done when:** CEO shell runs; enroll + pulse succeed against Tower 1 with
  operator gates you chose; public `tower1-public-smoke.sh` stays green without
  any Guardian-only public artifact; this `.mirl` is the canonical program text
  in git. Preview HTML requires `X-Guardian-Token` / `X-S25-Token` — it is not in
  the public MIR-L catalog.
}
